The CYD port of Pocket Tank: the MIT License, and what it covers

This licence covers the CYD port, LM's own work in this fork of Pocket Tank:

  - the files listed below, and
  - LM's changes inside upstream's files, as far as they can be separated
    from upstream's code.

It does NOT cover upstream's code - Pocket Tank, by StratoBuilds - which
stays under upstream's terms: the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
(LICENSE) from v0.3.9.3 on, the MIT License in NOTICE up to and including
v0.3.9.2. An upstream file the fork has changed is still upstream's file, and
stays under upstream's terms. NOTICE-CYD says what the layers mean together.

The CYD port's own files. The list is computed from git, not written from
memory: each is a path that no upstream commit or tag ever had, added by the
fork's own commits and renamed from no upstream file, with every line LM's
(CYD.md, "Licence", has the command and how to read it).

  CYD.md
  common/ui.h
  firmware/main/imu_chip.h
  firmware/main/orientation.h
  firmware/main/sdkconfig.rename
  firmware/main/sleep_setting.h
  firmware/sdkconfig.defaults.cyd
  tools/build_cyd.sh

Three more are LM's but for a few lines from upstream's MIT releases
(v0.3.9.2 and earlier). Those lines stay copyright MediaCutlet under the MIT
License in NOTICE, so these files are MIT throughout, and their headers name
both:

  firmware/main/imu_mpu6050.c     the I2C register helpers wr8 and rdn, TAG,
                                  the device handle and its configuration,
                                  from upstream's imu_port_qmi8658.c; two
                                  FreeRTOS includes from main.c
  firmware/main/orientation.c     the NVS open lines of upstream's
  firmware/main/sleep_setting.c   brightness.c, and three includes from
                                  persist_port_esp.c

Whoever reuses one of these three keeps MediaCutlet's copyright notice,
"Copyright (c) 2026 MediaCutlet", beside LM's below. The permission notice
is the same MIT text for both.

Every file above but CYD.md carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header;
CYD.md is documentation and is listed here only.

